#*: {{ja-usex|「[[てっきり]][[推し]]を[[自%分]]の[[妹]]とか[[言う|言っ]]てる'''イタい'''[[人]]かと[[思う|思っ]]てましたよ〜」|「^てっきり おし を じ%ぶん の いもうと と か いってる '''イタい''' ひと か と おもってました よ〜」|"I totally thought that you were just one of those '''embarrassing''' people who call their favorite idol their little sister or something!"}}
# {{lb|ja|obsolete}} [[wonderful]], [[pleasant]]

====Usage notes====
The desiderative suffix {{ja-r|たい}} is ultimately derived from this word. The sense of “wonderful” may have influenced this development.

The {{ss|ja|title={{lg|semantic shift|shift}}|type=p}} in meaning towards only meaning “painful” is similar to the changes of the word {{ja-r|すばらし.い|t=terrible→wonderful}} or of {{noncog|en|terrific}}, {{m|en|sick}}, and {{m|en|wicked}}, and contrary to {{m|en|awful}}.

